# UI Toolkit First (All Created UI)

**Any UI you create is UI Toolkit.** Not uGUI (`Canvas`, `Image`, `TextMeshProUGUI`, `MenuUiBuilder` runtime panels). Hard lock: `dark-matter-genesis-uitk-lock.mdc`.

The UITK cutover exists to **stop uGUI per-frame ticks**. Once UITK is working for a surface, fully retire that surface's uGUI ticking rather than dual-run forever. Do not destroy leftover uGUI until the new surface is complete and the user asks.

## Required stack

| Layer | Location / pattern |
|-------|-------------------|
| Layout | `Assets/UI Toolkit/Screens/<Screen>.uxml` |
| Styles | Screen `.uss` + `Assets/UI Toolkit/Themes/DarkMatterGenesis.uss` |
| Runtime | `Assets/UI Toolkit/Runtime/DMUiToolkit*.cs` (`MonoBehaviour` on a named `UIDocument` host) |
| Colors | `DarkMatterGenesisUiPalette` / Shift theme (`dark-matter-genesis-ui-palette.mdc`) |
| Naming | `DM` / `DMI` prefixes for new project UI types (`dm-naming-no-invector.mdc`) |

## Host documents (reuse — do not invent a second HUD root)

- **Gameplay HUD / journal chrome:** `UITK_Hud` (`DMUiToolkitHud`, `DMUiToolkitMenus`)
- **Main menu / pause modals:** `UITK_MainMenu`, `DMUiToolkitMenuPanels` siblings
- **Fullscreen overlays:** `DMUiToolkitOverlayDocument.Ensure(...)` (vignette, hazards, loading, optics, **pilot cluster**)
- **Panel settings:** share bootstrap `PanelSettings` via `DMUiToolkitBootstrap`
- **Do not** parent a second `UIDocument` under `UITK_Root` or assign it a different Panel Settings.

## UI Builder

- **Every `Hud.uxml` element stays visible in UI Builder.** Never hide HUD pieces with USS `display: none`.
- Hide unused hosts **only in C# at runtime** so textures/sprites can still be dropped on them in Builder.
- UI Builder Save must write **runtime UXML** (Editor Extension Authoring **off**) so Play shows the fonts, position, and color just saved.

## Gameplay HUD vs tilde

- Tilde / cinematic chrome hides **gameplay HUD only** (hotbar, minimap, compass, standby, XP, temp/hazards, leftover bars/crosshair/dots).
- Overlays that are not gameplay chrome (zone vignette, hit flash, menus) stay up unless the feature says otherwise.
- Defer unused overlay `EnsureHost` until first show (LevelUp, Dialogue, Craft, Death, etc.).
- Do not per-frame `Q()`, rebuild VisualElements, or `Find` for HUD ticks.

## Prototype combined HUD (`showPilotCluster`)

- Lower-right UITK cluster on `DMUiToolkitConfig.showPilotCluster`.
- **Existing HUD stays up** until the prototype is complete and the user asks to remove it.
- No background panel — only the minimap circle gets the map texture. Palette colors, not mockup orange/green.

## Settings Apply

- In-game Apply that reloads graphics: snapshot the live run, stay **paused on Settings**. Settings Back → pause. Pause Main Menu → title. Title Continue loads the real save. Do not dump into a blank no-UI game.

## Do

- Add UXML elements with stable `name=` ids; bind in C# with `root.Q<T>(...)`.
- Use USS classes (`dmg-*`) for layout and state — avoid inline styles except dynamic values.
- Wire input through existing bridges (`DMUiToolkitInputHost`, `GameplayKeyboardShortcuts`, Input System).
- Disable or hide legacy uGUI for the same surface when UITK drives it (`DMUiToolkitUguiRetirement` pattern).

## Do not

- Create new `Canvas` menu/HUD/popup hierarchies with `MenuUiBuilder`, TMP labels, or `GraphicRaycaster` stacks.
- Add new uGUI “fallback” panels “just in case” when `DMUiToolkitConfig.IsEnabled` — ship UITK only.
- Expand retired surfaces (wallet, legacy MainCanvas chrome) in uGUI.
- Let `MainCanvasFlow` re-enable uGUI HUD Canvas/Graphics after UITK owns HUD.

## Legacy uGUI

Existing uGUI under `MainCanvas` / Invector may remain until deliberately migrated. When **touching** a UI feature for new work, **extend or replace with UITK** — do not add parallel uGUI.

## Exceptions

Only build uGUI when the user **explicitly** requests legacy uGUI for that task, or the target is third-party package UI that cannot be UITK-wrapped yet (document why in the PR/commit note).
